---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="What IENN is, why it exists, and who it's working with.">
  <section class="section page-header-section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>About IENN</h1>
      <p class="section-intro" style="margin-left:0;">
        <strong>IENN</strong> — the <strong>Irish ESFRI Node Network</strong> — is a
        grassroots, cross-domain forum for Ireland's national nodes within
        European Strategy Forum on Research Infrastructures (ESFRI) Research
        Infrastructures. It is <strong>not an officially sanctioned body</strong>.
        It began as an open initiative formed by two of Ireland's existing
        ESFRI nodes, <strong>DARIAH-Ireland</strong> and <strong>ELIXIR-Ireland</strong>,
        to bring the country's ESFRI-facing communities into a single,
        coordinated conversation. As engagement and support grow across
        Ireland's research domains, we intend to pursue more formal
        recognition and structures over time.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Why IENN exists</h2>
      <ul class="about-list">
        <li>Act as an open, cross-domain forum connecting Irish researchers to a gateway to Europe.</li>
        <li>Reduce redundancy across Ireland's ESFRI-related investments.</li>
        <li>Ensure alignment on common technological and infrastructural needs across domains.</li>
        <li>Provide a unified, coordinated voice for Ireland's research domains in ESFRI-related matters.</li>
        <li>Collaborate on shared projects and initiatives, including the European Open Science Cloud (EOSC), EOSC Ireland, and INFRADEV.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-subtle">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Our goal</h2>
      <p>
        Our goal is to support researchers across all domains with
        well-provisioned research infrastructure, backed by ESFRIs that meet
        Ireland's needs with European and global solutions that actually
        work in practice.
      </p>
      <p>
        Part of that means aligning over metadata and standards — and
        especially <strong>FAIR data</strong> and <strong>open science</strong> —
        which we consider core to a healthy research ecosystem.
      </p>
      <p>
        ESFRIs also play an important role in Ireland's wider research
        infrastructure landscape: representing research needs and domains as
        <strong>EOSC Ireland</strong> is built up, and providing valuable
        context for national investment such as <strong>INSPIRE</strong> —
        Ireland's national research infrastructure investment programme
        (Department of Further and Higher Education, Research, Innovation
        and Science / Research Ireland).
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Stakeholders</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Research Ireland</strong> and the <strong>Department of
        Further and Higher Education, Research, Innovation and Science
        (DFHERIS)</strong> are key stakeholders in this effort.
      </p>
      <p>
        We're also working to engage and align with other government
        departments whose remits intersect with ESFRI infrastructure needs —
        for example the <strong>Department of Health</strong>, given the
        sensitive nature of health data and the EU's
        <strong>European Health Data Space (EHDS)</strong> and wider data
        space initiatives.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .about-list {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: var(--space-3);
      max-width: 760px;
      margin: 0;
      padding-left: 1.2rem;
    }

    .about-list li {
      color: var(--color-text);
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
